Acknowledgements
----------------
* GNOME Network Displays (https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-network-displays,
  GPL-3.0-or-later) was studied as a reference for how a Linux Wi-Fi Display
  source drives NetworkManager Wi-Fi P2P and the WFD RTSP M1–M7 exchange
  (source speaks first, MPEG-TS over RTP, keep-alives). No GND source code was
  copied or translated; this project's Python implementation was written from
  the public Wi-Fi Display specification. Interoperability facts adopted from
  observing GND: the WFD device-information flag value 0x0090 and the
  1080p30 fallback when a sink reports no usable modes.
* EVDI (https://github.com/DisplayLink/evdi; kernel module GPL-2.0, library
  LGPL-2.1) is used at runtime through the distribution packages
  `evdi-dkms` and `libevdi1`, loaded dynamically via ctypes. Not bundled.
* GStreamer, PipeWire, xdg-desktop-portal and NetworkManager are used at
  runtime under their own licenses. Not bundled.
